{"name":"Grey Area","hex":"#8f9394","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey area","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area intermediate between two mutually exclusive states or categories, where the border between the two is fuzzy or ill-defined.","A topic that is not clearly one thing or the other, that is open to interpretation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey_area"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Grey Area of Mute Records discography","blocks":[{"text":"The Grey Area is a Mute Records division founded in 1990 to restore and reissue the catalogue of artists who influenced Daniel Miller, head of Mute Records, and to reissue previous recordings of Mute artists.\nIn 1983, Mute had to partner with Industrial Records for the reissue of Throbbing Gristle albums. This division was created following the partnerships signed with Can and Cabaret Voltaire."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Grey_Area_of_Mute_Records_discography","wikidata":"Q99541429"},{"title":"Grey Area (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Grey Area is the third studio album by English rapper Little Simz, released on 1 March 2019 through Age 101 Music and AWAL."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Little_Simz_%E2%80%93_Grey_Area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_Area_(album)","wikidata":"Q61978178"},{"title":"Area","blocks":[{"text":"Area is the measure of a region's size on a surface. The area of a plane region or plane area refers to the area of a shape or planar lamina, while surface area refers to the area of an open surface or the boundary of a three-dimensional object. Area can be understood as the amount of material with a given thickness that would be necessary to fashion a model of the shape, or the amount of paint necessary to cover the surface with a single coat. It is the two-dimensional analogue of the length of a curve or the volume of a solid .\nTwo different regions may have the same area ; by synecdoche, \"area\" sometimes is used to refer to the region, as in a \"polygonal area\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Squaring_the_circle.svg/330px-Squaring_the_circle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area","wikidata":"Q11500"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG/500px-SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG/1280px-SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG/500px-SquareMeterQuadrat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A square metre quadrat made of PVC pipe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASquareMeterQuadrat.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Area_conversion_-_square_mm_in_a_square_cm.png/500px-Area_conversion_-_square_mm_in_a_square_cm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Area_conversion_-_square_mm_in_a_square_cm.png/500px-Area_conversi